# Architecture

## Application shell (do not break)

Live shell:

- Layout: `src/app/layout.tsx` — `SoundInit` + `DesktopLoggingInit` + `AuthProvider` → `AppDataProvider` → `AccessGate` → `AppShell`
- Sidebar: `components/sidebar.tsx` (hidden on auth lock screens and presentation mode)
- Feature pages only fill `{children}` inside the main area

## Routing

- **Single shell:** Next.js App Router — `src/app/**/page.tsx`
- Layout: `src/app/layout.tsx`; Sidebar: `components/sidebar.tsx`
- Tauri desktop loads static export from `out/` (same Next build; `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` from build-time env). Production targets: **Windows x86_64** and **macOS** (aarch64 + x86_64). No Linux desktop releases.

## Before changing shell or navigation

Read:

- `docs/PROJECT_SCOPE.md`
- `docs/ACCOUNTS.md` (auth, entitlements, cloud backup)
- `docs/DATA_ARCHITECTURE.md` (local vs R2)
- `docs/build-and-release.md` (Tauri Windows/macOS packaging)
- `PROJECT_RULES.md`
- `AGENTS.md`

## Next.js 16

- Turbopack is default for `next dev`
- Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` when APIs are ambiguous — this is not standard Next.js 14/15
- Do not flag `proxy.ts` as a misnamed middleware file on Next.js 16 projects

## Never

- Replace `src/app/layout.tsx` with a standalone feature page
- Remove or hide Sidebar navigation items
- Create a second application layout or entry point
